This document serves as a technical master-guide for implementing the visualization and reasoning engine used in the **NXT Humans** research system. It focuses on the specific configuration of **Gemini 3 Pro**, **Nano Banana (Gemini 3 Pro Image)**, and **Veo 3**.

---

# NXT Humans AI Implementation Guide

## 1. Core Architecture Strategy
The application uses a "Dual-Engine" approach:
- **Logic Engine (`gemini-2.5-flash`):** Handles high-speed reasoning, stateful chat history, and structured JSON output.
- **Visual Engine (`gemini-3-pro-image-preview` / `veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview`):** Handles high-fidelity corporate illustrations and animations.

---

## 2. Visual Generation (Nano Banana Pro)
We use `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` to generate the signature "Laci Jordan" aesthetic.

### Logic: Aspect Ratio & Prompt Injection
The service dynamically injects style constraints based on the intended use-case (Persona vs. Slide).

```typescript
// From services/geminiService.ts
export const generateImage = async (prompt: string, aspectRatio: string = "16:9", refImageBase64?: string) => {
    const ai = new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: process.env.API_KEY });

    // Aesthetic Constraints
    const styleDirectives = aspectRatio === "1:1" 
        ? "Style: Modern, professional illustration in the style of Laci Jordan. Bold vibrant colors, flat design, clean lines."
        : "Style: Modern, professional corporate illustration in the style of Laci Jordan. Bold vibrant colors, flat design, clean lines. Context: Business research insights.";

    const negativeConstraints = "Do not include: photorealism, 3D render, dark mode, gritty texture, messy scribbles, illegible text, complex shading, clutter, cinematic lighting.";

    const finalPrompt = `Depict specifically: ${prompt}. Ensure all visual elements are extremely related to this description. ${styleDirectives} ${negativeConstraints}`; 

    const response = await ai.models.generateContent({
      model: 'gemini-3-pro-image-preview',
      contents: { parts: [{ text: finalPrompt }] },
      config: {
        imageConfig: {
          aspectRatio: aspectRatio as any,
          imageSize: "1K"
        }
      }
    });
    // ... logic to extract inlineData
};
```

### Visual Consistency (Reference Images)
When generating scenes for a specific persona, we pass the persona's portrait as `inlineData` to maintain character consistency.

```typescript
// Sending a reference image to Nano Banana
const parts = [
    { inlineData: { mimeType: 'image/png', data: personaBase64 } },
    { text: "Depict this persona using a laptop in a brightly colored office. Maintain strict character consistency." }
];
```

---

## 3. Video Animation (Veo 3.1)
We use `veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview` to animate static frames for the video storyboard.

### Polling Implementation
Video generation is asynchronous. We use a `while` loop to poll the operation status.

```typescript
export const generateSceneVideo = async (prompt: string, imageBase64?: string) => {
    const ai = new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: process.env.API_KEY });

    // Create the generation operation
    let operation = await ai.models.generateVideos({
        model: 'veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview',
        prompt: `Animate strictly: ${prompt}. Modern illustration animation style. Flat 2D motion.`,
        image: imageBase64 ? { imageBytes: imageBase64, mimeType: 'image/png' } : undefined,
        config: { numberOfVideos: 1, resolution: '720p', aspectRatio: '16:9' }
    });

    // Poll for completion (max 2.5 minutes)
    let attempts = 0;
    while (!operation.done && attempts < 30) {
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 5000));
        operation = await ai.operations.getVideosOperation({ operation });
        attempts++;
    }

    const downloadLink = operation.response?.generatedVideos?.[0]?.video?.uri;
    return `${downloadLink}&key=${process.env.API_KEY}`;
};
```

---

## 4. Robust JSON Reasoning (Gemini Pro)
To prevent `JSON Parse Errors` when the model generates large research datasets, we use a specialized "Repair" utility.

### The JSON Repair Stack
This handles truncated responses by closing open braces/brackets if the model hits a token limit.

```typescript
function tryRepairJson(jsonString: string): string {
    let stack: string[] = [];
    let inString = false;
    let cleaned = jsonString.trim().replace(/```json|```/g, '');

    for (let char of cleaned) {
        if (char === '"') inString = !inString;
        if (!inString) {
            if (char === '{' || char === '[') stack.push(char === '{' ? '}' : ']');
            else if (char === '}' || char === ']') stack.pop();
        }
    }

    while (stack.length > 0) cleaned += stack.pop();
    return cleaned;
}
```

### Structured Output with Schema
For deterministic results (like the PRD or Journey Map), we enforce a strict `responseSchema`.

```typescript
const schema: Schema = {
    type: Type.OBJECT,
    properties: {
        methodology: { type: Type.STRING },
        themes: {
            type: Type.ARRAY,
            items: {
                type: Type.OBJECT,
                properties: {
                    name: { type: Type.STRING },
                    description: { type: Type.STRING },
                    isCrossDocument: { type: Type.BOOLEAN }
                },
                required: ["name", "description"]
            }
        }
    },
    required: ["methodology", "themes"]
};
```

---

## 5. Human-in-the-Loop "Ground Truth"
A critical UX feature is the ability to edit data mid-stream. We inject manual user edits back into the AI's "Ground Truth" using the `updateContext` method.

```typescript
// Forcing the model to respect manual user edits
async updateContext(contextLabel: string, data: any) {
    const prompt = `SYSTEM UPDATE: The user has MANUALLY EDITED the ${contextLabel}. 
    Use the following JSON as ground truth for all future steps. 
    Discard previous interpretations of this specific data: \n\n ${JSON.stringify(data)}`;

    await this.chatSession.sendMessage({ message: prompt });
}
```

---

## 6. Prompt Engineering Standards
- **Tone:** "Elite Chief Experience Officer (CXO) and Expert Ethnographer."
- **Transparency:** Every response must include a `methodology` field with tags like `[PHASE]`, `[INSIGHT]`, and `[CORRECTION]`.
- **Evidence:** Strict requirement for verbatim citations: `ALWAYS provide a CITATION quote for every insight.

